<appfunctions>
    <appfunction>
        <id>com.oplus.gallery.openabilitypage.PhotoFunctions#findPhotos</id>
        <enabledByDefault>true</enabledByDefault>
        <description>Searches for images and videos based on a user's text query.
 This function is designed to parse the user's request for specific details like Time (specific), Location (city and country), Person (user-named),
 Album (user-created albums in gallery), Other attributes (smart categories such as food, buildings, animals, etc.), Text in photos (OCR),
 File name search, and Natural language description (multimodal search) to perform a refined search.
 This enables more accurate and precise search results.
 To achieve the best results, when such information is mentioned in the user query, you should extract and populate the following fields as much as possible:
 Time (supports absolute time), city, country, countryCode, person, album,
 label (including child labels, guide labels, special labels), ocrText, fileName,
 queryString (must generate a detailed semantic query).
 **IMPORTANT:** The findPhotos tool returns machine-level URIs (content://...) intended exclusively for the backend UI widget. When processing these results, you must extract only the total count of the items found.
 Limit your text output to a natural, friendly conversational summary. Acknowledge that you searched OPPO Photos and state the number of items found. Ensure your final response consists entirely of standard natural language words and numbers.</description>
        <parameters>
            <dataTypeMetadata>
                <id>unused</id>
                <isNullable>false</isNullable>
                <type>8</type>
            </dataTypeMetadata>
            <id>unused</id>
            <isRequired>true</isRequired>
            <name>keyword</name>
            <description>The keyword to search for. this parameter Only includes the parts of the user input that are relevant to photo search. It should retain only descriptive content, such as: Location, Time, Person, Album name, Other attributes, OCR text, File name, Natural language description Command words must be removed, such as: find, show, get. The query does not support multiple keyword combinations.</description>
        </parameters>
        <response>
            <id>unused</id>
            <valueType>
                <dataTypeReference>com.oplus.gallery.openabilitypage.PhotoFunctions$FindPhotosResponse</dataTypeReference>
                <id>unused</id>
                <isNullable>false</isNullable>
                <type>11</type>
            </valueType>
            <description>The search results.</description>
        </response>
        <functionId>com.oplus.gallery.openabilitypage.PhotoFunctions#findPhotos</functionId>
    </appfunction>
